verdicts.suggested_fix:
Keep the conclusion that the exact sampler gives no speed-up with Fast drafts, but fix the numbers:
- whole-state acceptance: at most about 1e-21;
- ||Delta||: 19-84 at the sigma 0.937 state and 47-203 at sigma 0.833;
- rel-L2: 17-78% and 14-47%;
- per-position reuse: about 45-91%;
- Fast: about 0.9 s per forward;
- SPEC_AR: measured 0.91x.

Make the target definition match the runs in flight. Either redefine T_H as T_H^c9 (9-latent window, decoded-latent start image, pose offset) or drop --ctx 9 from q173. Drop --resident, which peaks at 78.7 GB and OOMs whenever the GPU is shared. Replace "no output yet" with the specstep_n012c9 jar s1234 results.

Report the target-parallel gain as systems parallelism, not as speculative sampling:
- about 2.4-2.9x for full-prefix T_H0, but only with conditioning precomputed off the node-0 GPU;
- about 2.4x (about 130 s) for c9;
- compare it against plan->render in both wall-clock and GPU-seconds.

Make the Fast forward concurrent with Base under DLOCK so SPEC_AR reaches about 1.0x. Drop CS-AR while we have 4 GPUs. If it is still wanted, first measure Base's node-1 x0 change under a context swap offline (2 forwards per chunk) against the 1.7% threshold. Fix the C1 residual tolerances: per transition, mean +/-0.0018 and variance +/-0.0026; pooled over 36 transitions, +/-0.0003 and +/-0.0004.

Keep the design. Its mathematics holds (exact w.r.t. T_PR under A1-A6). Before claiming exactness, close these gaps:
(1) Domain-separated seeding. Derive every generator seed by hashing a role tag plus indices, e.g. int(sha256(('u',seed,c,j)))%2**63, ('zeta',seed,c,j,call_idx), ('tail',seed,c,i), ('xi_eps',seed), ('plan',seed). Assert that all seeds used in a run are pairwise distinct. Never reuse the raw clip seed for more than one role.
(2) Non-finite guard in the coupler: where D_p is not finite, set z_p = mT_p + sd*eps_p.
(3) Hard asserts:
- --start 0, and SPEC_NODES == all stochastic transitions of K, plus a per-chunk counter that every transition was coupled;
- policy == never; bguide/polish/seam/handoff/corr-*/sem off;
- base_lora, mixed_lora and noise_corr off;
- the target CFG taken from --spec-cfg only (drop a.bguide_cfg from base_x0_at);
- env vars SPECWM_PLUCKER_REF and SPECWM_NO_FLASH identical across arms and logged.
(4) Fix the target spec:
- tail[0] = s3 exactly;
- for T_AR-kv, either build a high-expert KV cache or declare that node 0 uses the low expert;
- write the mp4 round-trip and the window-image rule into T;
- rename the claim to 'exact w.r.t. T_PR', not 'unbiased w.r.t. Base'.
(5) Make the target function arm-invariant:
- clone U(P) and z before handing them to the Base thread;
- do the window-image VAE decode on dev1 or precompute it;
- set cudnn.deterministic=True and benchmark=False.
(6) Replace 'verified by calibration z-scores' with three plumbing tests that can actually catch A3-A5 violations:
- (a) Oracle-draft test. Run arm A with Fast executing normally, so all its side effects happen, but feed mT as the draft mean to the coupler. Every position is accepted, and the output must be bitwise identical to arm B under common random numbers.
- (b) Determinism. Two arm-A runs with the same seed must be bitwise identical.
- (c) Replay. Log (z_{c,j}, X_<c, the RNG keys) from arm A, recompute mT in a clean target-only process, and require bitwise (or <= 1e-6) equality.
Keep the z-tests as coupler checks only, with the threshold set for 1664 tests.
(7) Protocol: report all seeds; re-runs must be seeded replays; blind the video review.
